1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,016
TiffinTally turns a pasted WhatsApp export into tomorrow's tiffin counts. This take is the restyled app on this machine, still on the rules path.

2
00:00:08,391 --> 00:00:17,391
This public copy has no model key, so the on-device rules do the reading. A paste stays in this browser session and is not written to disk.

3
00:00:17,813 --> 00:00:27,813
These names are made up. Ravi, Priya, Karan and Pooja order lunch. Karan also asks for one plate for roommate Tanvi. Vikram claims a payment.

4
00:00:27,813 --> 00:00:37,829
Two lines are uncertain on purpose. Ravi adds a peanut-allergy note. Priya asks to cancel one thali after a roommate left, without saying whose plate.

5
00:00:38,204 --> 00:00:46,219
The cook's name is Aunty, so a message from Aunty is not turned into an order. The cutoff is 10:00 pm. These lines are all before it.

6
00:00:46,219 --> 00:00:49,219
Processing now. Python applies the messages in time order for tomorrow. Nothing is sent to WhatsApp.

7
00:00:49,719 --> 00:00:58,735
The banner says Rules (regex) only. No model was called, so every count on this sheet came from the pattern rules.

8
00:00:59,094 --> 00:01:09,110
The morning brief is text only. There is no audio, because no voice key is configured. It says seven lunch thalis, and it names the onion and rice notes.

9
00:01:09,110 --> 00:01:19,110
It also says two messages are still waiting. Some of those plates are already inside the total. The line that was not counted stays out until the cook confirms it.

10
00:01:19,469 --> 00:01:28,485
Seven lunch packs, no dinner, and no cancellation applied. Priya's cancel was not subtracted, because it never said which plate to remove.

11
00:01:28,860 --> 00:01:37,860
Notes the rules recognised go on the station alert: no onion for Pooja, rice instead of roti for Priya, and no onion from Ravi's second line.

12
00:01:38,235 --> 00:01:48,250
Human Review still shows both uncertain lines. Ravi's allergy note was packed and labelled, and it stays here because 'peanut allergy' is not a standard modification.

13
00:01:48,250 --> 00:01:57,266
Priya's cancel stays in review and was not applied. In demo mode, Save Correction changes this sheet only. It does not write a file.

14
00:01:57,625 --> 00:02:07,641
The labels split Karan's two plates into Karan 1 and Tanvi 1. Ravi is 2, Pooja is 2, and Priya is 1. The peanut words sit on Ravi's label.

15
00:02:07,704 --> 00:02:17,735
The dues ledger uses the same plate counts, at 80 rupees a thali. It does not bill a meal twice, and it does not invent a customer who did not write in.

16
00:02:18,094 --> 00:02:29,110
Vikram's 1,500 rupees is a payment claim, not a receipt. The balance stays open until the cook checks the real account and presses Confirm received. This recording does not press it.

17
00:02:29,469 --> 00:02:37,485
Copy Draft only copies a reminder onto the clipboard. The app has no WhatsApp sending key, so it never sends a message.

18
00:02:37,485 --> 00:02:45,485
That is the demo: a paste, the review queue, the prep sheet, and the ledger. Made-up names, rules only, nothing stored.
